Fixed a gate parity broke: `npm run check:orchestrator` exited 1 with no verdict on
both this tip and the manus-parity baseline (a5d0cf3), with the identical crash
(runFinalRepair -> all providers failed/cooled -> longcat:cloud HTTP 404). Cause: the
smoke harness's testCfg() called loadConfig() without overriding coding/failover, so the
real defaults applied (coding enabled; six failover providers) and a worker coding turn
escaped the injected fake client to the real provider chain. Since this gate passed
before parity landed the coding router (C17 recorded 114/114), it was a real regression
in the harness, not merely upstream noise. src/scripts/check-orchestrator.ts now sets
cfg.coding = { enabled: true, chain: [], logEdits: false } and cfg.failover = { providers: [] }
in testCfg(): with no coder in the chain the router falls back to the harness's fake
client for every turn. No assertion was weakened or removed; the smoke is unchanged in
what it verifies, only hermetic in where a coding turn resolves. Now exits 0 at
"orchestrator smoke: PASS (114/114)", and the full `npm run verify` exits 0.

