One inherited failure, proven NOT caused by this merge
-----------------------------------------------------
  src/agent/__tests__/toolDescriptions.test.ts
  "keeps every coding-profile tool either linted or explicitly pending"
  -> AssertionError: suggest_plan is neither registered nor listed in
     PENDING_CODING_TOOLS

Provenance (on the manus-parity lineage, independent of D17):
  - b6e908f (C3) added the coding tool profile and this lint test together.
  - 25da47e (D4) then added "suggest_plan" to CODING_PROFILE.tools in
    src/agent/taskToolScope.ts but did NOT add it to the test's
    PENDING_CODING_TOOLS, and the test's registry does not include
    createPlanTools (which is what registers suggest_plan).
  - The test therefore asserts a contradiction that D4 introduced on parity.

Proof the failure is not merge-induced (three independent checks):
  1. The test file, taskToolScope.ts and planTools.ts are byte-identical to
     97c53d7 (`git diff 97c53d7 HEAD -- <file>` is empty for each).
  2. Computed the test's full transitive relative-import closure (85 files).
     Only 2 of the 85 differ from parity at all (src/agent/events.ts,
     src/agent/prompt.ts, i.e. D17's own additions), and neither is reachable
     from the failing assertion: no file in the closure references
     suggest_plan or planTools. The assertion depends only on
     CODING_PROFILE.tools and the modules the test's own registry builds.
  3. Decisive experiment: reverted those 2 files to their parity bytes so all
     85 closure files were exactly parity's, and re-ran the test -> it still
     fails with the same assertion. Restored the files afterwards (blob hashes
     confirmed back at HEAD's).

This is a pre-existing upstream defect on manus-parity, outside D17's diff and
outside every file D17 touched. It was left untouched: "fixing" it would mean
either weakening/editing another task's (D4's) test or changing D4's production
tool profile, both of which the task rules forbid.

